// =============================================================================
//  triage-session.json — the ONE file shared by the three steps of the loop
// =============================================================================
//
//  Location:  D:\Gabriel\OneDrive\Claude\Workspace\Personal Assistance\email-triage\triage-session.json
//
//  Step 1  pa-email-triage        (Cowork skill)  → CREATES the file
//  Step 2  triage-review.html     (Gabriel)       → EDITS decisions; Confirm or Skip ONE GROUP at a time
//  Step 3  pa-email-triage-save   (Cowork skill)  → once no group is pending, APPLIES every "reviewed" group
//
//  This is an annotated example, not a formal JSON Schema. Every key is listed
//  with WHO writes it. The general rule for all three steps: load the whole
//  JSON, mutate only the keys you own, write the whole JSON back — never drop a
//  key you don't understand.
//
//  ─── Groups / tabs (exactly two — there is NO session-level status) ─────────
//  The file holds two independent review queues ("groups"). Each has its own
//  status; nothing else in the file carries a status. `groups` has exactly the
//  keys "personal" and "shared" — never a third one.
//
//     group key   | tab label         | which emails            | which tasks
//     ------------+-------------------+-------------------------+-------------------------------------
//     "personal"  | Personal          | source !== "gmail"      | group !== "Gabriel & Arina"
//     "shared"    | Gabriel & Arina   | source === "gmail"      | group === "Gabriel & Arina"
//
//  Group status lifecycle (one per group):
//     "pending-review"        → written by step 1; the tab is editable on the page
//     "reviewed"              → step 2, Confirm & Save on that tab; tab locked
//     "skipped"               → step 2, Skip on that tab; tab locked (Reopen puts it back to pending)
//     "processed"             → step 3, after applying a "reviewed" group
//     "processed-with-errors" → step 3, same but at least one item failed
//  "skipped" groups stay "skipped" forever (step 3 never touches them).
//  Step 3 refuses to run while EITHER group is still "pending-review".
//
//  ─── Fixed vocabularies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  groups   : "Work" | "Personal" | "Gabriel & Arina" | "New Ideas"
//  tags     : base list "Admin" | "Finance" | "Health" | "Property" | "Dev" | "Research" | "Errand"
//             PLUS every Gmail user label (see "Gmail labels ≡ Notion Tags" below)
//  category : "Important" | "FYI" | "Not Important"
//  emailAction (non-tracked email — chosen from the category):
//             Not Important → "archive"                              (locked)
//             FYI           → "archive" (default) | "flag"
//             Important     → "create-task" (default) | "flag" | "archive"
//  emailAction (tracked email, i.e. existingTaskUrl set — no category):
//                             "update-task" (default) | "complete-task" | "cancel-task"
//
//  What each emailAction means for step 3 — the action decides INBOX vs ARCHIVE only:
//     "archive"        archive the email                                   (leaves inbox)
//     "flag"           keep the email in the inbox (page label: "Keep in inbox")
//     "create-task"    create Notion task from  decision.task ?? suggestedTask ; keep in inbox
//     "update-task"    apply existingTasks[].decision.edits of the matched task; keep in inbox
//     "complete-task"  set matched task to Done       AND archive the email
//     "cancel-task"    set matched task to Cancelled  AND archive the email
//  Every email therefore ends up either in the inbox or archived.
//  Never delete an email, never reply, never draft.
//
//  ─── Star / flag is its OWN property: decision.flagged ──────────────────────
//   • `isFlagged`        (step 1) = current state: Gmail has label STARRED / Outlook flagStatus "flagged"
//   • `decision.flagged` (step 2) = wanted state after the save, for EVERY email (both mailboxes)
//   • It is independent of the action: an archived email may stay starred, an
//     inbox email may be unstarred. Page default = isFlagged; choosing a
//     keep-in-inbox action ("flag" / "create-task" / "update-task") switches it ON
//     as a convenience, Gabriel can toggle it back.
//   • Step 3: flagged !== isFlagged → Gmail add/remove STARRED, Outlook flag_email
//     "flagged" / "notFlagged"; equal → nothing. Applied for every action, after
//     the archive/keep step. Outcome "starred" | "unstarred" | "flagged" | "unflagged".
//
//  ─── Gmail labels ≡ Notion Tags ─────────────────────────────────────────────
//  Gmail (shared mailbox) labels and the Notion "Tags" multi-select share ONE
//  namespace: identical names, character for character.
//   • Step 1 records the USER-CREATED labels only (never system labels such as
//     INBOX, UNREAD, STARRED, IMPORTANT, SENT, DRAFT, SPAM, TRASH, CATEGORY_*):
//       - `gmailLabels`      = every user label that exists in the mailbox
//       - `emails[].labels`  = the user labels currently on that email
//     and sets `suggestedTask.tags = labels` for Gmail suggestions.
//   • Step 2 lets Gabriel toggle labels on the email (`decision.labels`) and
//     edit tags on the task. For a Gmail email linked to a task (create-task or
//     tracked) the two are ONE value — the page copies whichever side was
//     edited last onto the other, so in the written file
//     decision.labels == (decision.task ?? suggestedTask).tags  (create-task)
//     decision.labels == existingTask tags after decision.edits (tracked).
//   • Step 3 applies BOTH sides of every reviewed Gmail email:
//       - Gmail:  add    = decision.labels − labels
//                 remove = labels − decision.labels
//         (create a missing Gmail label first; do this for every action, archive included)
//       - Notion: write the task tags as usual (decision.task.tags / suggestedTask.tags /
//         decision.edits.tags), creating any missing option on the Tags property first.
//   • `systemLabels` (step 1, gmail): every OTHER label on the message — the
//     Gmail system labels such as IMPORTANT, UNREAD, CATEGORY_UPDATES,
//     CATEGORY_PROMOTIONS … — EXCEPT INBOX and STARRED, which are modelled by the
//     action and decision.flagged. Read-only: shown muted on the page, never
//     edited by the page, never written back to Gmail by step 3.
//   • Outlook emails have no labels: `labels` / `systemLabels` / `decision.labels` are absent.
//
//  Other hard rules:
//   • Gmail-sourced tasks (suggestedTask / decision.task of a gmail email) are
//     ALWAYS group "Gabriel & Arina"; Outlook-sourced ones NEVER are.
//   • existingTaskUrl, when set, must equal the url of one existingTasks[] entry.
//   • Task descriptions (notes): everything ABOVE the literal line
//         -- auto comment --
//     is Gabriel's own text and must never be modified. Everything BELOW is
//     Claude's briefing — one "DD Mon: summary" line per email matched to the
//     task — and is regenerated on every run. Step 3 writes edits.notes as a
//     whole string; the page has already built it with this split preserved.
// =============================================================================
{
  // ── Session-level ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Step 1. ISO-8601 timestamp of when the triage ran. The page shows its age.
  "generatedAt": "2026-08-29T08:00:00.000Z",

  // Step 1 (informational). Which mailboxes were actually fetched this run —
  // e.g. ["outlook"] when the Gmail connector was down. The page ignores it.
  "mailboxes": ["outlook", "gmail"],

  // Step 1. All USER-CREATED labels of the shared Gmail (system labels excluded).
  // The page offers these (plus the base tags) as toggles on Gmail emails and as
  // tag checkboxes in the task editor.
  "gmailLabels": ["Travel", "House", "Kids"],

  // Per-group status — THE thing step 3 keys off. Exactly two keys. Step 1 must
  // write both as "pending-review" (the page will create them if missing).
  // NOTE: there is deliberately no top-level "status" key; if one is found in an
  // old file the page deletes it (together with reviewedGroups / skippedGroups /
  // top-level processedAt) after migrating it into `groups`.
  "groups": {
    "personal": {
      "status": "pending-review",   // see lifecycle above
      "reviewedAt": null,           // step 2: ISO timestamp of Confirm or Skip on this tab (null again after Reopen)
      "processedAt": null           // step 3: ISO timestamp when this group was applied
    },
    "shared": {
      "status": "pending-review",
      "reviewedAt": null,
      "processedAt": null
    }
  },

  // ── Emails ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Step 1 writes every field except `decision` (may be omitted; the page
  // fills defaults) and `outcome` (step 3 only). REQUIRED from step 1:
  // id, source, category, summary. One entry per inbox email considered.
  "emails": [
    {
      // Mailbox message id. Used for the deep link on the page AND by step 3 to
      // act on the email (archive / flag / labels), so it must be the real id for that source.
      "id": "AAMkAGI2...",
      "source": "outlook",          // "outlook" → Personal tab · "gmail" → Gabriel & Arina tab
      "sourceId": "outlook:AAMkAGI2...",   // step 1: "<source>:<id>"; becomes the Notion "Source ID" property (duplicate check in step 3)
      "from": "Jane Doe <jane@example.com>",
      "subject": "Rates notice due 15 Sep",
      "date": "2026-08-28T22:14:00.000Z",
      "summary": "Council rates $612 due 15 Sep; pay via BPAY.",   // Claude's 1-2 line summary; also feeds the auto comment
      "isFlagged": false,           // step 1: current flag (Outlook) / star (Gmail) state
      // (no `labels` / `systemLabels` keys: Outlook email)

      // Step 1's classification; Gabriel can change it on the page. Drives the
      // default emailAction. Ignored (not shown) when existingTaskUrl is set.
      "category": "Important",

      // null for a NEW topic. Set to the Notion url of a matching open task to
      // mark the email as "tracked" — it then only offers update/complete/cancel.
      "existingTaskUrl": null,

      // Step 1's proposed task for Important emails (null when nothing to suggest,
      // and always null for tracked emails). Same shape as decision.task.
      "suggestedTask": {
        "title": "Pay council rates ($612)",
        "notes": "BPAY, due 15 Sep. See email.",
        "group": "Personal",        // fixed list; Gmail emails → must be "Gabriel & Arina"
        "tags": ["Finance", "Admin"],// base tags ∪ Gmail labels, 0..n; Gmail emails → must equal `labels`
        "dueDate": "2026-09-15",    // "YYYY-MM-DD" or "" for none
        "link": "https://outlook.live.com/mail/0/inbox/id/AAMkAGI2..."   // email deep link, stored on the task
      },

      // Step 2 (the page) owns this block. Step 1 may omit it entirely.
      "decision": {
        "emailAction": "create-task",   // vocabulary above; ALWAYS one of the allowed values for this email
        "isTask": true,                 // derived: emailAction === "create-task". Never read it, read emailAction.
        "flagged": true,                // step 2: wanted flag/star state (see header). Step 3 diffs vs isFlagged.
        // Gabriel's edited copy of the task to create. null means "use suggestedTask
        // unchanged". When emailAction is "create-task" the page guarantees that at
        // least one of decision.task / suggestedTask is non-null (it builds a
        // fallback from subject + summary if neither existed).
        // Always null when emailAction !== "create-task".
        "task": null
      },

      // Step 3 only — the page never writes it and shows it read-only in the
      // processed summary. A short human string, e.g. "archived",
      // "flagged", "task created", "task updated", "labels +Travel −House",
      // "FAILED: <reason>" (anything matching /fail/i is shown red). Absent until processed.
      "outcome": "task created"
    },
    {
      // ── A GMAIL email that becomes a new task ──
      "id": "18f3a2b9c0d1e2f3",
      "source": "gmail",
      "sourceId": "gmail:18f3a2b9c0d1e2f3",
      "from": "TAP Air Portugal <noreply@flytap.com>",
      "subject": "Fare alert: Lisbon 12 Oct",
      "date": "2026-08-29T01:10:00.000Z",
      "summary": "Fare alert for Lisbon 12 Oct at $1,450 return.",
      "isFlagged": false,
      "labels": ["Travel"],          // step 1: USER labels on the email right now (editable, == task tags)
      "systemLabels": ["IMPORTANT", "CATEGORY_UPDATES", "UNREAD"],   // step 1: the rest, minus INBOX/STARRED (read-only)
      "category": "Important",
      "existingTaskUrl": null,
      "suggestedTask": {
        "title": "Check Lisbon fare $1,450 (12 Oct)",
        "notes": "TAP alert — compare with Qantas.",
        "group": "Gabriel & Arina",  // forced for Gmail
        "tags": ["Travel"],          // == labels (step 1 rule)
        "dueDate": "",
        "link": "https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#inbox/18f3a2b9c0d1e2f3"
      },
      "decision": {
        "emailAction": "create-task",
        "isTask": true,
        "flagged": true,                      // create-task switched it on; Gabriel left it on
        // Gabriel added the "House" label on the page → the task's tags follow,
        // so the page wrote an edited copy of the task with the same tags.
        "labels": ["Travel", "House"],        // step 2: desired Gmail labels after save (step 3 diffs vs `labels`)
        "task": {
          "title": "Check Lisbon fare $1,450 (12 Oct)",
          "notes": "TAP alert — compare with Qantas.",
          "group": "Gabriel & Arina",
          "tags": ["Travel", "House"],        // == decision.labels
          "dueDate": "",
          "link": "https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#inbox/18f3a2b9c0d1e2f3"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      // ── A TRACKED Gmail email: already has a Notion task ──
      "id": "18f3a2b9c0d1e999",
      "source": "gmail",
      "sourceId": "gmail:18f3a2b9c0d1e999",
      "from": "Arina <arina@example.com>",
      "subject": "Re: Flights to Lisbon",
      "date": "2026-08-29T03:40:00.000Z",
      "summary": "Arina prefers the 12 Oct departure; asks to book by Friday.",
      "isFlagged": true,
      "labels": ["Travel"],
      "systemLabels": ["IMPORTANT"],
      "category": "Important",    // present but not shown/used for tracked emails
      "existingTaskUrl": "https://www.notion.so/Book-Lisbon-flights-1a2b3c4d",   // must match existingTasks[].url
      "suggestedTask": null,
      "decision": {
        "emailAction": "update-task",   // update-task | complete-task | cancel-task only
        "isTask": false,
        "flagged": false,               // Gabriel unstarred it on the page although it stays in the inbox
        "labels": ["Travel", "Errand"], // Gabriel toggled "Errand" → mirrored into the task's decision.edits.tags below
        "task": null
      }
    }
  ],

  // ── Existing Notion tasks ───────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Step 1 writes the OPEN Notion tasks it considered relevant (at least every
  // task referenced by an existingTaskUrl, ideally all open tasks so Gabriel
  // can complete/edit them from the page). Step 1 writes every field except
  // `decision` (page) and `outcome` (step 3). Values must be the CURRENT Notion
  // values — the page diffs against them and only records changed fields.
  "existingTasks": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.notion.so/Book-Lisbon-flights-1a2b3c4d",   // Notion page url = the task's identity
      "title": "Book Lisbon flights",
      // Full description as in Notion. Gabriel's text above the marker, Claude's
      // dated briefing below it (see hard rules). May have no marker yet.
      "notes": "Compare TAP vs Qantas.\n-- auto comment --\n27 Aug: Arina asked for options before 15 Oct.",
      "status": "Not started",     // Notion status as-is (informational)
      "group": "Gabriel & Arina",  // fixed list; decides the tab this task appears in
      "tags": ["Travel"],          // current Notion tags (names shared with Gmail labels)
      "dueDate": "2026-09-05",     // "YYYY-MM-DD" or ""
      // Step 1 extras copied from Notion (Link / Source / Source ID properties).
      // Informational; the page preserves them untouched, step 3 does not need them.
      "link": "https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#inbox/18f2...",
      "source": "Gmail (G&A)",     // Notion Source option: "Outlook" | "Gmail (G&A)" | "Manual"
      "sourceId": "gmail:18f2...",

      // Step 2 owns this block. Step 1 may omit it.
      "decision": {
        "complete": false,         // true ⇒ step 3 sets the task to Done      (mirrors emailAction "complete-task")
        "cancel": false,           // true ⇒ step 3 sets the task to Cancelled (mirrors emailAction "cancel-task")
        // null = nothing changed. Otherwise ONLY the fields that differ from the
        // values above are present; step 3 applies exactly these.
        // `notes` is the full new description (Gabriel's part + refreshed auto comment).
        // `tags` here == decision.labels of every Gmail email tracked by this task.
        "edits": {
          "notes": "Compare TAP vs Qantas.\n-- auto comment --\n27 Aug: Arina asked for options before 15 Oct.\n29 Aug: Arina prefers the 12 Oct departure; asks to book by Friday.",
          "tags": ["Travel", "Errand"],
          "dueDate": "2026-09-04"
        }
      },

      // Step 3 only, e.g. "updated", "completed", "cancelled", "untouched", "FAILED: …"
      "outcome": "updated"
    }
  ],

  // ── New tasks added by Gabriel on the page ──────────────────────────────
  // Step 1 writes an empty array (or omits it). Step 2 appends. Step 3 creates
  // each one in Notion; the tab a task belongs to is decided by its `group`.
  // No source restriction applies (typed by hand, not derived from an email).
  "newTasks": [
    {
      "title": "Renew passport",
      "notes": "Expires Feb 2027 — book appointment.",
      "group": "Personal",
      "tags": ["Admin"],
      "dueDate": "",
      "outcome": "created"        // step 3 only
    }
  ]
}

// =============================================================================
//  Step-by-step responsibilities
// =============================================================================
//
//  STEP 1 — pa-email-triage (creates the file; overwrite any previous session)
//    • generatedAt; groups = { personal: {…pending…}, shared: {…pending…} } — exactly
//      those two keys, each { status: "pending-review", reviewedAt: null, processedAt: null }.
//      NO top-level status key.
//    • gmailLabels: every user-created label of the shared Gmail.
//    • mailboxes: which connectors were fetched.
//    • emails[] (id, source, sourceId, from, subject, date, summary, isFlagged,
//      category, existingTaskUrl | null, suggestedTask | null;
//      gmail only: labels = user labels, systemLabels = all other labels minus
//      INBOX/STARRED) — no decision / outcome.
//      isFlagged: Gmail = message has STARRED; Outlook = flagStatus "flagged".
//    • existingTasks[] with current Notion values (incl. tags, link, source,
//      sourceId) — no decision / outcome
//    • newTasks: []
//    • Gmail suggestions: group "Gabriel & Arina" and tags == labels.
//
//  STEP 2 — triage-review.html (mutates in place, per tab)
//    • Fills every emails[].decision (incl. decision.labels for gmail) and
//      existingTasks[].decision, appends newTasks. Keeps Gmail labels and the
//      linked task's tags identical.
//    • Confirm & Save on a tab: groups.<tab> = { status: "reviewed", reviewedAt: now,
//      processedAt: null } for THAT TAB ONLY, then writes the whole file.
//      Skip on a tab: same with status "skipped". Reopen (skipped → pending) sets
//      reviewedAt back to null. The other tab is never touched.
//    • Refuses to write if groups.<tab>.status on disk is not what it last saw.
//    • Never writes processedAt or any outcome field.
//    • Migrates legacy files on load (top-level status / reviewedGroups /
//      skippedGroups / processedAt → groups, then deletes those keys; any group
//      other than personal / shared is dropped).
//
//  STEP 3 — pa-email-triage-save (mutates in place, per group)
//    • GATE: if groups.personal.status or groups.shared.status is "pending-review",
//      stop and change nothing — Gabriel must Confirm or Skip every tab first.
//    • For EACH group whose groups.<g>.status === "reviewed":
//        – emails of that group: perform decision.emailAction (table above);
//          for "create-task" create decision.task ?? suggestedTask in Notion
//          (Status "Not started", Link, Source, Source ID = email.sourceId; if a
//          task with that Source ID already exists → outcome "skipped-duplicate").
//          Then star/flag: decision.flagged !== isFlagged → Gmail STARRED add/remove
//          or Outlook flag_email; every action, archived emails included.
//          Gmail emails: also apply the USER label diff (labels → decision.labels);
//          never touch systemLabels.
//        – existingTasks of that group: apply decision.edits (only the keys
//          present; create missing Tags options first), then
//          decision.complete → Done / decision.cancel → Cancelled.
//        – newTasks of that group: create in Notion.
//        – stamp `outcome` on every item touched (string; put "FAILED: …" on errors).
//        – set groups.<g>.status = "processed" (or "processed-with-errors" if any
//          item failed) and groups.<g>.processedAt = now.
//    • Never touch a "skipped" group (leave its status "skipped") or one that is
//      already "processed" / "processed-with-errors".
//    • Do NOT add a top-level status (or any other session-level status) — the
//      two group statuses are the only ones. Write the whole file back.
// =============================================================================
